# Plant Supply image handling

When adding or updating images on `plant-supply.html`:

- **Do not crop** images to fit fixed layout boxes (`object-fit: cover`, `background-size: cover`, forced `min-height` on media frames).
- **Adapt the layout** to each image's natural aspect ratio: use `<img>` with `width: 100%`, `height: auto`, and `object-fit: contain`.
- Media containers should use `height: fit-content` (not fixed min-heights) so the section grows/shrinks with the asset.
- Hero and full-bleed banners: wrap image + overlay in a `*-stage` container sized by the image; overlay text sits absolute over the image bounds only.
- Follow the same pattern as `architectural-harmony.html` intro media and `white-glove-service.html` beyond section.

```css
/* ✅ Preferred */
.ps-fit-image {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  object-fit: contain;
  object-position: center;
}

/* ❌ Avoid on plant-supply */
object-fit: cover;
background-size: cover;
min-height: clamp(...); /* on media-only columns */
```
